0,Galarrwuy Yunupingu - Wikipedia,https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galarrwuy_Yunupingu,"Galarrwuy Yunupingu (30 June 1948 – 3 April 2023), also known as James Galarrwuy Yunupingu and Dr Yunupingu, was an Indigenous Australian activist who was a leader in the Aboriginal Australian community. He was involved in Indigenous land rights throughout his career. He was a Yolngu man of the Gumatj clan, from Arnhem Land in the Northern Territory. He was the 1978 Australian of the Year.",Gurindji,Australian
1,From Little Things Big Things Grow - Wikipedia,https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/From_Little_Things_Big_Things_Grow,""" From Little Things Big Things Grow "" is a protest song recorded by Australian artists Paul Kelly & The Messengers on their 1991 album Comedy, and by Kev Carmody (with Kelly) on his 1993 album Bloodlines. It was released as a CD single by Carmody and Kelly in 1993 but failed to chart. The song was co-written by Kelly and Carmody, and is based on the story of the Wave Hill walk-off (Gurindji ...",Gurindji,Australian
2,Song for the Gurindji | AIATSIS corporate website,https://aiatsis.gov.au/blog/song-gurindji,"Here they continued their struggle for another eight years. During this time the Gurindji cause garnered support from a wide range of groups in Australian society, including the union and student movement. Finally, on 16 August 1975, Prime Minister Gough Whitlam handed over leasehold title to the Gurindji’s ancestral land.·",Gurindji,Australian
3,Gurindji Blues by Galurrwuy Yunupingu and featuring Vincent Lingiari,https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=EdLIlyhLewI,Irish Music Session Etiquette for Beginners (and Bodhran players) Simon Cowell Made Him Sing A Cappella! What Happened Next SHOCKED Everyone! 😮,Gurindji,Australian
4,Karungkarni Band - GURINDJI MAN - YouTube,https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=2xIfgGrrEEo,This winning song at the Vamp Camp Garma Festival Songwriting Competition tells the story of the epic Gurindji struggle for land rights starting with a strik...,Gurindji,Australian
5,Festival — Gurindji Aboriginal Corporation RNTBC,https://www.gurindjicorp.com.au/festival,"Every August, people from across Australia gather on Gurindji country for the Gurindji Freedom Day Festival, a celebration of Land Rights, self-determination and community success. The Gurindji people invite you to journey into the heart of the Northern Territory for a unique and memorable weekend of arts, culture, music and sports.",Gurindji,Australian
6,Ted Egan – Gurindji Blues Lyrics - Genius,https://genius.com/Ted-egan-gurindji-blues-lyrics,"Gurindji Blues Lyrics: In the 1960s, Australia heard, for the first time, the expression 'land rights' / As two quite different tribal groups sought official recognition / Of their age old ...",Gurindji,Australian
7,The Soundtrack of Reconciliation - Australian Institute of Music,https://aim.edu.au/news/the-soundtrack-of-reconciliation/,"Ted Egan – “Gurindji Blues” Right alongside were the non-indigenous artists singing from the social justice songbook. From the Goanna Band’s ‘Solid Rock,’ Midnight Oil’s landmark album ‘ Diesel and Dust,’ to Paul Kelly’s stark truth in ‘Bicentennial,’ here was a potent soundtrack that called for Reconciliation. While politics ducked for cover on Australia’s First ...",Gurindji,Australian
8,Music - Paul Kelly: Getting to the heart of things - Australia Explained,https://australia-explained.com.au/music/music-paul-kelly-getting-to-the-heart-of-things/,"music review Music - Paul Kelly: Getting to the heart of things By Loretta Barnard on July 24th, 2023 In 1991, Paul Kelly and Murri singer-songwriter Kev Carmody wrote a song that chronicled the story of the Gurindji strike, also known as the Wave Hill Walk-Off.",Gurindji,Australian
